---
source: system/tests/help_snapshots.rs
expression: "help_output(\"dmesg\")"
---
Print or control the kernel ring buffer

Usage: dmesg [OPTIONS]

Options:
  -f, --facility <FACILITY>        Restrict output to the given comma-separated list of facilities
  -H, --human                      Enable human-readable output (implies --color and --reltime)
  -k, --kernel                     Print only kernel messages
  -l, --level <LEVEL>              Restrict output to the given comma-separated list of levels
  -L, --color [<COLOR>]            Colorize the output (auto, always, never)
  -r, --raw                        Print raw message buffer (with priority prefix)
  -T, --ctime                      Display human-readable timestamps
  -t, --notime                     Do not print timestamps
  -u, --userspace                  Print only userspace messages
  -w, --follow                     Wait for new messages
  -W, --follow-new                 Wait for and print only new messages
  -x, --decode                     Decode facility and priority to human-readable prefixes
  -d, --show-delta                 Show time delta between messages
  -e, --reltime                    Display local time and delta in human-readable format
      --time-format <TIME_FORMAT>  Time format: raw, ctime, reltime, delta, notime, iso
  -h, --help                       Print help
